       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** metformin 2550 mg per dose, three times daily, which is **7,650 mg/day**.\n- **Why it's a problem:** the maximum recommended daily dose of metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release. A single 2,550 mg dose equals the whole daily maximum. At 7,650 mg/day, the risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis is serious.\n\nYou may have meant **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day. Or you may have meant a lower dose, such as 500 mg BID or 1,000 mg BID.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. Once you do, I'll enter it right away. For example, I can enter metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals."
